From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:45:33 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: "Allow for this task" on the agent's question

At access level "ask", a six-link moodboard took a dozen "Allow"s. The
card now offers Allow once, Allow for this task and Deny (Always allow
stays as the link). Allow for this task lets this agent's connection
(its name and bridge process) act without asking on every site,
including ones the person is signed in to, as the card says, until it
reconnects, Stop is pressed, access changes, or 30 minutes pass. Its
waiting questions are answered with it. Another connection is still
asked. The question goes through a new AskAgentAction (choice string);
AskAgent stays for the first "may it connect" question.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
